# S-021 DEFECTS D-9 of obs_parse_av1_header / obs_parse_av1_packet: the reference reads bytes
# beyond the end of its input (1-2 bytes after the last OBU) when an OBU header, its size field
# or the sequence header is cut off, when the sequence header does not end exactly at its
# trailing one-bit, and obs_parse_av1_header reads data[0] of an empty input.
# The runner places the input directly before an inaccessible page, so each such case is
# recorded as "crash". REQUIRED behaviour: obs_parse_av1_header returns 0 and sets no header
# (the output line "av1_header ret=0 header=unset").
# The cut-off inputs that the reference rejects cleanly are in 41-av1-header-obus.
# empty input
av1_header -
# one byte: OBU header with has_size=1 but no size field
av1_header 0a
# extension flag without the extension byte
av1_header 0e
# size field cut off (LEB128 continuation bit)
av1_header 0a80
# sequence header one bit too short: syntax needs one more bit than present
av1_header 0a0a00000042abbfc37709d0
# sequence header whose last bits are wrong
av1_header 0a0b00000042abbfc37709d0e0
# sequence header OBU then a lone OBU header byte with has_size=1
av1_header 0a0b00000042abbfc37709d0010a
# sequence header OBU then a lone OBU header with extension flag
av1_header 0a0b00000042abbfc37709d0010e
